    "title": "Timberwolves vs. Thunder: Live updates, highlights for Sunday's game",
    "text": "Updated March 15, 2026, 1:52 p.m. CTThe Oklahoma City Thunder will host the Minnesota Timberwolves on Sunday. This will be the fourth matchup of the season. OKC has lost two of three. Last time out, OKC fell in a frustrating loss on Jan. 29.The Thunder (52-15) have won seven in a row. They outlasted the Boston Celtics in a 104-102 win on Thursday. Shai Gilgeous-Alexander had 35 points and nine assists as he passed Wilt Chamberlain for the NBA record of longest 20-point streak ever.Meanwhile, the Timberwolves (41-26) grabbed a badly-needed 127-117 win over the Golden State Warriors on Friday. Anthony Edwards had 42 points and eight rebounds to avoid an upset.For live updates of the Thunder's game against the Timberwolves, please regularly check back to this post: End 3Q: Thunder 80, Timberwolves 76Good third quarter for the Thunder. Especially the latter parts. They finally retook the lead and found some momentum. Gilgeous-Alexander has 10 points and nine assists. Playing within the flow of the game. Will be interesting to see if he prioritizes keeping his 20-point streak alive. Regardless, let's see if OKC can win another close contest against a high-quality opponent. 3Q, 3:25 left: Timberwolves 71, Thunder 68Gilgeous-Alexander rejects Gobert on the dunk attempt. Williams gets the layup on the other end. Timberwolves call a timeout. Half: Timberwolves 53, Thunder 47Feels like the Thunder wasted some golden chances to pull ahead. They're plus-18 in the shot attempt category, but it just hasn't mattered. The Timberwolves have made up for it by being superbly efficient. Randle and Dosunmu have been awesome. Meanwhile, Gilgeous-Alexander only has four points. Ugly stuff. 2Q, 3:50 left: Thunder 43, Timberwolves 37The good news is the Thunder are forcing an unreal number of turnovers. The bad news is they can't cash in on the other end. OKC has taken 48 shot attempts compared to Minnesota's 31. End 1Q: Thunder 23, Timberwolves 22After a hot start, the Thunder really cooled off. They allowed the Timberwolves to get back into it despite losing the turnover battle so far. The OKC crowd was not happy that Edwards got away with high-five contact on Gilgeous-Alexander's jumper. 1Q, 6:50 left: Thunder 12, Timberwolves 5Mitchell draws the shooting foul on McDaniels. Thunder call a timeout. Minnesota is 2-of-10 from the field to start, so great job by OKC's defense. Starting lineups:The Thunder will start Shai Gilgeous-Alexander, Ajay Mitchell, Lu Dort, Chet Holmgren and Isaiah Hartenstein. The Timberwolves will start Anthony Edwards, Donte DiVincenzo, Jaden McDaniels, Julius Randle and Rudy Gobert.What channel is Timberwolves vs. Thunder game on today? Time, TV scheduleTV Channel: ABCStart time: 12 p.m. CTWhere to watch Timberwolves vs. Thunder on livestreamWatch Timberwolves vs. Thunder live on Fubo (free trial)Timberwolves vs. Thunder injury updatesThunder: Jalen Williams (hamstring strain) is out. Isaiah Hartenstein (calf contusion) is questionable. Nikola Topic (G League assignment) is out. Branden Carlson (back strain) is out. Brooks Barnhizer (G League two-way) is out. Thomas Sorber (torn ACL) is out.Timberwolves: Anthony Edwards (knee soreness) is questionable. Julian Phillips (G League assignment) is out. Joan Beringer (G League assignment) is out. Enrique Freeman (G League two-way) is out. Zyon Pullin (G League two-way) is out.Thunder 2025-26 scheduleTuesday, Mar. 17 at MagicWednesday, Mar. 18 at NetsSaturday, Mar. 21 at Wizards",
